// Pins the success side of the frame-count ceiling that
// 31_deep_recursion.lox already pins the failure side of: 1022 nested
// calls is the deepest depth that stays under src/vm.h's FRAMES_MAX (1024)
// on native (see 31_deep_recursion.lox's own header for the arithmetic),
// and the JVM counter (runtime/jvm/src/lox/LoxClosure.java) must agree.
//
// The two probes together catch an off-by-one in either direction: a
// counter that starts too low lets 31_deep_recursion.lox (1023) wrongly
// succeed; a counter that starts too high makes this probe (1022) wrongly
// fail. Neither probe alone can see the other's mistake.
//
// This probe does not bind the bootstrap interpreter. Under the call depth
// exception of spec/04-semantics.md, the bootstrap interpreter may support a
// lower call depth than 1022, and a program that needs more may raise
// StackOverflowError. The probe has no STATUS line, so the spec-probe gate
// does not run it on the bootstrap.
fun down(n) {
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    down(n - 1);
    return 0;
}
print down(1022);
